      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "Instructor: So it's configuration file time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "We do have a bunch of files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 8.61,
          "en": "and let's go through them to understand what we got here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "Now please note over time some files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 13.8,
          "en": "and the content of some files can change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.8,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "but the general idea of course is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "Now let's start with the .editorconfig.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "This is a file which in the end is picked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 25.38,
          "en": "up by some editors by some IDEs like Visual Studio Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.38,
          "end": 30.24,
          "en": "And it basically tells the editor how to, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "do indentation in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "so that it can override your user default settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "or the the IDE default settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 41.13,
          "en": "and make sure that the code in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.13,
          "end": 43.38,
          "en": "actually is the same for all users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.38,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "across the entire world, no matter which editor they use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "So this is simply a code style thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "This of course does not affect the way Angular works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "or how you write Angular code it really just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.543,
          "en": "influences how the code looks like and is formatted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.543,
          "end": 64.8,
          "en": "\".prettierrc\", by the way is kind of related to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.8,
          "end": 67.44,
          "en": "but is not part of a default Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.44,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "at least not at the point of time I'm recording this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "This is a file I added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "to tell this auto formatting tool prettier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "which I'm using behind the scenes to basically use single",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "instead of double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "So in the end this should work together with .editorconfig.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 83.257,
          "en": "Now I skipped .gitignore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.257,
          "end": 86.877,
          "en": ".gitignore of course matters if you are working with Git,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.877,
          "end": 89.7,
          "en": "Git is a source control tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 92.1,
          "en": "It helps you create code snapshots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "and go back to older code snapshots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 96.66,
          "en": "if you mess something up and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.66,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "and you can learn more about Git",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "with the attached Git starting resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "and .gitignore is a file which basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "tells get which files it can ignore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "which files you don't want to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "with Git because they will be regenerated frequently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "like node modules which you generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 115.713,
          "en": "by running npm install and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 119.43,
          "en": "Now the angular.json file is a bit of a more complex file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "This manages your entire project configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 123.75,
          "en": "and we will come back to that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.75,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "Let's skip it for now and let's move on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "to the browserslist instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "The browserslist file is an amazing file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 134.16,
          "en": "This configuration file is picked up by the Angular CLI when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.16,
          "end": 137.25,
          "en": "you build your project for production and it basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.25,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "tells the Angular CLI which browsers you want to support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "with your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now the Angular CLI takes this information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.98,
          "en": "about which browsers you want to support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.98,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "In my case, you for example that I don't want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "support Internet Explorer 9 to 11, which you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 153.06,
          "en": "would have to change here, remove not as you see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.06,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "If you do want to support it and to see, I will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "use this information for example, to adjust your CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "and prefix them to support all these browsers and also to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "load the right polyfills and create the right code bundles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "that include those polyfills and more on Polyfills",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 175.47,
          "en": "and what the CLI does with them later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.47,
          "end": 178.71,
          "en": "But this really allows you to control which browsers your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.71,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "application supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "And of course you want to be as restrictive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 182.16,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "as possible here and not as open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "as possible because that will ultimately lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "to less code which your users have to download.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 191.79,
          "en": "So if you know you don't have to support Internet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 195.21,
          "en": "Explorer 9 to 11, well you should not support it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "The Angular framework by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "does support those browsers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 203.91,
          "en": "but still excluding them can make sense to ship less code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 207.69,
          "en": "The karma.conf file here, that's a file which is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.69,
          "end": 211.04,
          "en": "for testing in the end for unit tests where Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.04,
          "end": 214.47,
          "en": "the Angular CLI uses Karma behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 216.69,
          "en": "And unless you really know what you're doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "you should leave it the way it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 220.29,
          "en": "It allows you to fine tune",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 220.29,
          "end": 223.083,
          "en": "how your tests are executed and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.37,
          "end": 227.46,
          "en": "package-lock.json is a file which is generated based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.46,
          "end": 229.68,
          "en": "on your package.json file, which in turn is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.68,
          "end": 233.19,
          "en": "a file that manages the packages your project uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.19,
          "end": 235.17000000000002,
          "en": "and the versions of those packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 235.17000000000002,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "Now with my current theme, I see that's a bit hard to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 240.15,
          "en": "So let me quickly switch this to a default dark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "plus theme where this is a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 244.02,
          "en": "Now what do we have here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 244.02,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "Now this package.json file has a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "of scripts we can execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 250.5,
          "en": "We can also use just the NG command though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 252.66,
          "en": "so we can ignore this behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "This uses the NG command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 256.05,
          "en": "More interesting are the dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 256.05,
          "end": 257.58,
          "en": "and depth dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "I did talk about them early in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 263.61,
          "en": "In the end, these are the third party packages our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 263.61,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "uses to build our application and to run successfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 269.91,
          "en": "That includes all the different parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 269.91,
          "end": 273.6,
          "en": "of the Angular framework, rxjs for observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 273.6,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "and then some dependencies of the Angular framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "But we also got some development dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 281.58,
          "en": "which are tools we only need to build our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 283.83,
          "en": "So this is not code which will be part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 283.83,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "of our running application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "These will be tools that help us build the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "efficiently. That's the Angular CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 292.32,
          "en": "And then a couple of tools used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 292.32,
          "end": 295.56,
          "en": "by the CLI for compiling and optimizing the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 297.18,
          "en": "We got Karma for testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 297.18,
          "end": 298.2,
          "en": "We got Typescript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 298.2,
          "end": 302.34,
          "en": "for compiling Typescript to JavaScript and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 302.34,
          "end": 307.34,
          "en": "Now you use this file by running npm install in the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 307.98,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "or command prompt navigated into your project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 312.9,
          "en": "And here I'm just using the built-in one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 312.9,
          "end": 315.48,
          "en": "which you get with terminal, new terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 315.48,
          "end": 317.07,
          "en": "And this will basically create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 317.07,
          "end": 318.69,
          "en": "that node modules folder based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 318.69,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "on the dependencies mentioned here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 323.28,
          "en": "It will also de generate a package-lock.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 323.28,
          "end": 325.56,
          "en": "which stores the exact versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 325.56,
          "end": 328.17,
          "en": "of your third party dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 328.17,
          "end": 330.15,
          "en": "because here in package.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 330.15,
          "end": 335.15,
          "en": "you specify some minimum requirements and some flexibility.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 335.46,
          "end": 337.38,
          "en": "And then once you do run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 337.38,
          "end": 340.89,
          "en": "you lock in certain exact versions which are saved in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 340.89,
          "end": 341.94,
          "en": "And last but not least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 341.94,
          "end": 344.15999999999997,
          "en": "we got the tsconfig files down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 344.15999999999997,
          "end": 347.01,
          "en": "Now we see 3 tsconfig.json files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 347.01,
          "end": 349.44,
          "en": "this configures the TypeScript compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 349.44,
          "end": 352.65,
          "en": "And if you took my understanding TypeScript course here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 352.65,
          "end": 355.32,
          "en": "on Udemy, which of course is not a hard requirement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 355.32,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "you know what you can set there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 359.07,
          "en": "The official TypeScript documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 361.14,
          "en": "of course is another great place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 361.14,
          "end": 362.64,
          "en": "Now unless you know what you're doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 362.64,
          "end": 364.41,
          "en": "you can leave the default here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 364.41,
          "end": 367.44,
          "en": "But there you can set certain interesting things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 367.44,
          "end": 370.95,
          "en": "For example, you can add strict mode by setting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 370.95,
          "end": 373.74,
          "en": "to true and now TypeScript will be way more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 373.74,
          "end": 376.38,
          "en": "restrictive regarding what you're allowed to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 376.38,
          "end": 377.79,
          "en": "in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 377.79,
          "end": 381.09,
          "en": "This can be a pro and can be a con depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 381.09,
          "end": 383.04,
          "en": "on which kind of code you're writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 385.74,
